a word sequence can be decomposed into the product of conditional next word distributions:\n","$$ P(w_{1:T} | W_0 ) = \\prod_{t=1}^T P(w_{t} | w_{1: t-1}, W_0) \\text{ ,with }  w_{1: 0} = \\emptyset, $$\n","\n","and $W_0$ being the initial *context* word sequence. The length $T$ of the word sequence is usually determined *on-the-fly* and corresponds to the timestep $t=T$ the EOS token is generated from $P(w_{t} | w_{1: t-1}, W_{0})$.\n","\n","We will give a tour of the currently most prominent decoding methods, mainly *Greedy search*, *Beam search*, *Top-K sampling* and *Top-p sampling*.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"x27KpiMdI223"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"dMHpLhCbkFl4"},"source":["Based on: https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/llm_tutorial\n","\n","In this section, we will generate our own movie... with the help of an LLM!\n","\n","We will use a Qwen3 model, which means that we will have to re-tokenize what we input to the model with the model's specific tokenizer.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Choosing the model"],"metadata":{"id":"I1nncj6KH_Nt"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Huggingface hosts many pretrained and finetuned models on many text and vision tasks. For this exercise we are using an open-source and very small LLM of the Qwen3 family, Qwen3-1.7b (1.7 billion parameters): https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B\n","\n","Models on Huggingface are free to use, but some of them (LLaMA, Mistral, Gemma, etc.) may need an account and a (free) permission form to access."],"metadata":{"id":"0Jo_j0RQIBLV"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"LZKVI75jju2F","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":241,"referenced_widgets":["437ffa24622a460382c23ffc978dbc2e","36d270b430804d0ebb7da77db9aed242","cdc498b7d5e148b1a4f1365e8c77a53c","83c702bb0a2e42f387d72371477a5829","c54b8856912c47d9aa6770d8c917a5e0","b5621c93f67c43fe8d4e0a326ba3b482","f88f0f7c7402462c95135874fabdde00","6c643a367f134c92ad50ce35a